  "id": "DrugBank_DB00959 - MONDO_6547",
  "verbalization": "Methylprednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Exanthem (disease) through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Methylprednisolone may be associated with Exanthem via the use of Hydrocortisone Acetate, which is indicated for Exanthem. This implies that Methylprednisolone could potentially contribute to the development of Exanthem through a mechanism involving corticosteroid use. Additionally, Methylprednisolone is linked to Inherited Isolated Adrenal Insufficiency Due To Partial Cyp11a1 Deficiency, which is associated with Prednisolone, further suggesting a possible role of corticosteroids in the manifestation of Exanthem. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for corticosteroid use to influence the immune system and lead to the development of Exanthem. The evidence is supported by the clinical indication of corticosteroids in the treatment of Exanthem, although the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
